  "notes": [
    "Each viseme is a local feathered WebP sprite extracted from the dedicated character rig sheet.",
    "The base emotional face remains active during speech; the mouth is rendered independently.",
    "This is a production-usable raster 2.5D rig, not a binary .riv deformation rig.",
    "v1.6 adds independent fixed face windows for left/right eyes and brows, each driven without replacing the full emotional frame.",
    "Blinking swaps only the eye windows to the blink expression frame; gaze is a bounded local translation; brows use bounded vertical/rotational motion.",
